{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q424680","formula":"C₉H₁₆N₃O₁₃P₃","hill":"C9H16N3O13P3","elements":["H","C","N","O","P"],"composition":{"C":9.0,"H":16.0,"N":3.0,"O":13.0,"P":3.0},"names":{"en":"DCTP"},"descriptions":{"en":"Deoxycytidine triphosphate (dCTP) is a nucleoside triphosphate that contains the pyrimidine base cytosine. The triphosphate group contains high-energy phosphoanhydride bonds, which liberate energy when hydrolized. DNA polymerase enzymes use this energy to incorporate deoxycytidine into a newly synthesized strand of DNA. A chemical equation can be written that represents the process: (DNA)n + dCTP ↔ (DNA)n-C + PPi That is, dCTP has the PPi (pyrophosphate) cleaved off and the dCMP is incorporated into the DNA strand at the 3' end."},"fame":18,"pubchemCid":65091,"mass":467.16,"charge":0,"smiles":"C1[C@@H]([C@H](O[C@H]1N2C=CC(=NC2=O)N)COP(=O)(O)OP(=O)(O)OP(=O)(O)O)O","inchikey":"RGWHQCVHVJXOKC-SHYZEUOFSA-N","iupac":"[[(2R,3S,5R)-5-(4-amino-2-oxopyrimidin-1-yl)-3-hydroxyoxolan-2-yl]methoxy-hydroxyphosphoryl] phosphono hydrogen phosphate","classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"molecule","source":"pubchem","ref":"65091","atoms":44,"license":"PubChem (NIH), public data"},"structure":{"kind":"molecule","atoms":[{"x":1.426,"y":2.297,"z":0.157,"el":"P"},{"x":4.077,"y":1.281,"z":-0.623,"el":"P"},{"x":4.551,"y":-1.369,"z":0.582,"el":"P"},{"x":-1.209,"y":-1.047,"z":0.868,"el":"O"},{"x":-0.371,"y":-3.689,"z":-0.432,"el":"O"},{"x":0.846,"y":0.83,"z":0.514,"el":"O"},{"x":2.656,"y":2.012,"z":-0.852,"el":"O"},{"x":-5.149,"y":-2.007,"z":0.313,"el":"O"},{"x":0.302,"y":2.951,"z":-0.806,"el":"O"},{"x":1.789,"y":3.138,"z":1.346,"el":"O"},{"x":3.664,"y":-0.156,"z":-0.012,"el":"O"},{"x":4.713,"y":2.06,"z":0.642,"el":"O"},{"x":4.963,"y":1.215,"z":-1.832,"el":"O"},{"x":3.455,"y":-2.527,"z":0.848,"el":"O"},{"x":5.365,"y":-1.91,"z":-0.705,"el":"O"},{"x":5.3